.NET runtime
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of the .NET runtime's class library and of its native globalization
library, as they are at the v10.0.0 tag, are ported to .NET Framework 4.8 and
compiled into InstallerClean.Core, which every download carries. They are how a
path is read, joined and made full; how a file or folder is found, read, moved,
deleted and listed, and a folder made; how a search pattern is matched; how a
Windows error becomes an exception; how a registry key is listed; how a command
line is quoted for a new process, and the exception a refused start carries;
how a proxy is taken from the variables that name one;
how the machine's architecture is read; how a culture is named in the language
of the window; how names are sorted in a culture, through the ICU Windows ships; the dictionary, sequence, string, stream, ASCII, Math,
environment and timing members .NET Framework 4.8 lacks; and the text of the
messages its exceptions carry.

  https://github.com/dotnet/runtime

They are in these files in src/InstallerClean.Core/: Helpers/PathText.cs,
Helpers/FullPaths.cs, Helpers/Win32Marshal.cs, Helpers/RegistryNames.cs,
Helpers/RegistryData.cs, Helpers/ProxyFromVariables.cs,
Helpers/CommandLineArguments.cs, Helpers/Durations.cs, and in Compatibility/,
FrameworkFile.cs, FrameworkFileInfo.cs, FrameworkFileSystem.cs,
FrameworkFileSystemEnumerable.cs, FrameworkFileSystemName.cs,
FrameworkFileSystemInfo.cs, FrameworkDirectory.cs, FrameworkDirectoryInfo.cs,
FrameworkFileStream.cs, FrameworkStreamExtensions.cs,
FrameworkStringExtensions.cs, FrameworkCollectionExtensions.cs,
FrameworkEnumerable.cs, FrameworkEnvironment.cs, FrameworkMath.cs, Ascii.cs,
FrameworkArgumentException.cs, FrameworkArgumentOutOfRangeException.cs,
ConfigureAwaitOptions.cs, TaskCompletionSource.cs, FrameworkTask.cs,
FrameworkProcess.cs, FrameworkRuntimeInformation.cs,
FrameworkCultureDisplayName.cs, WindowsIcu.cs and FrameworkCollation.cs;
in src/InstallerClean/Helpers/CollatedSort.cs, which also follows the list
sort of WPF, and src/InstallerClean/Helpers/WindowChromeExtensions.cs, which
shows a window's system menu as WPF's SystemCommands does (WPF:
https://github.com/dotnet/wpf, MIT, the same copyright); and, for the tests,
src/InstallerClean.Tests/Compatibility/TestFramework.cs.

